&lt;pre&gt;LGTM3; very excited to see these landing.

On Wednesday, August 12, 2026 at 8:09:40 AM UTC-7 Rick Byers wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; LGTM2
&gt;
&gt; On Wed, Aug 12, 2026 at 11:06 AM 'Dan Clark' via blink-dev &lt;
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="d4b6b8bdbabff9b0b1a294b7bca6bbb9bda1b9fabba6b3"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; That plan sounds good. LGTM1 to ship in 154, provided we continue to 
&gt;&gt; address any concerns or feedback that come in up to that point.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, August 12, 2026 at 3:04:40 AM UTC-7 &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="0d637f627e682323234d6e657f626064786023627f6a"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; 
&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Update:
&gt;&gt;&gt; Using the new Github stacked PR feature, we now have a stack of 
&gt;&gt;&gt; non-draft PRs at &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12758"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12758&lt;/a&gt; in the last 
&gt;&gt;&gt; week.
&gt;&gt;&gt; It is being reviewed by Mozilla folks. We've found a few issues and 
&gt;&gt;&gt; fixed them as we went along, but nothing so far is a design/API change
&gt;&gt;&gt; (those changes were regarding some error conditions and edge cases).
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Apple folks will likely review this later in August as folks are on OOO.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; I am suggesting again to ship this in M154 (branching at end of August), 
&gt;&gt;&gt; allowing spec reviewers ample time to raise objections or make additional 
&gt;&gt;&gt; API changes until then (or after shipping, which is likely fine for the 
&gt;&gt;&gt; kind of edge-case/error handling cases that come up at this stage of 
&gt;&gt;&gt; review).
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Monday, August 3, 2026 at 5:14:51 PM UTC+1 Noam Rosenthal wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; On Mon, Aug 3, 2026 at 5:12 PM 'Dan Clark' via blink-dev 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="3557595c5b1b1b1b75565d475a585c40581b5a4752"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote: 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; Thanks Noam! I saw this news that might be helpful here: 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-30-stacked-pull-requests-are-now-in-public-preview/"&gt;https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-30-stacked-pull-requests-are-now-in-public-preview/&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;  
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Thanks I saw that just the other day! Good coincidental timing :) 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; -- 
