&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Extend+Experiment%5C%3A+Digital+Credentials+API+%5C%28issuance+support%5C%29%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Extend Experiment: Digital Credentials API (issuance support)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Alex+Russell%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Alex Russell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260824" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:03:33 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;This is an uncomfortably long OT end-to-end. If you're able to ship before 
the end of this extension, I would encourage you to do so.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

Also, why would this issue present a breaking change? Wouldn't it be 
possible to ship now and then add interoperable extensions on top of the 
shipped surface?:

  &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c-fedid/digital-credentials/issues/382"&gt;https://github.com/w3c-fedid/digital-credentials/issues/382&lt;/a&gt;

Why aren't we launching instead of extending the OT? Is there really *no* 
useful OT feedback?

Best,

Alex


