&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+Request.isReloadNavigation+attribute%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Request.isReloadNavigation attribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Chris+Harrelson%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Chris Harrelson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260429" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 29 Apr 2026 08:21:03 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;BTW this issue explains the rationale for this feature:
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524&lt;/a&gt;. A comment on that thread
indicates a real website that needs it:
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524#issuecomment-314870317"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524#issuecomment-314870317&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

I think it's about different cache invalidation for reloads vs not, under
the heuristic that the user wants to reset things when reloading.

