&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Prototype%5C%3A+Prefetch+activation+beacon%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Intent to Prototype: Prefetch activation beacon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22%27Jiacheng+Guo%27+via+blink%5C-dev%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;'Jiacheng Guo' via blink-dev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260513" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 13 May 2026 00:34:03 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;*Contact emails*
&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="e285cccccca2858d8d858e87cc818d8f"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;

*Explainer*
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

*Specification*
*No information provided*

*Summary*
The on-prefetch-activation HTTP response header enables servers to specify
a telemetry endpoint that the browser notifies when a prefetched resource
is used for navigation. Developers gain a reliable signal to measure the
precision and performance impact of their prefetch strategies.

*Blink component*
Blink&gt;Loader&gt;Preload
&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ELoader%3EPreload%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ELoader%3EPreload%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;

*Web Feature ID*
Missing feature

*Motivation*
The API is proposed for a reliable measurement of whether a prefetch page
is activated. This allows precise visit statistics for the prefetched page
without cache interference.

*Initial public proposal*
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WICG/proposals/issues/284"&gt;https://github.com/WICG/proposals/issues/284&lt;/a&gt;

*Goals for experimentation*
None

*Requires code in //chrome?*
False

*Tracking bug*
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://b.corp.google.com/issues/499814382"&gt;https://b.corp.google.com/issues/499814382&lt;/a&gt;

*Launch bug*
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://launch.corp.google.com/launch/4468679"&gt;https://launch.corp.google.com/launch/4468679&lt;/a&gt;

*Estimated milestones*

M150

*Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5118934710878208?gate=5175566203486208"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5118934710878208?gate=5175566203486208&lt;/a&gt;

