&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; This features adds a new opaque type for use with storage and uniform 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; buffers and workgroup variables. It allows the data in those variables to 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; be reinterpreted as other types. This is useful for both type-punning data 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; and logically sub-dividing a variable into multiple parts. For ease-of-use 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; and safety, the opaque type can only be operated on by new built-in 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; functions. The reinterpretation can only occur on the opaque type. This 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; maintains flexibility, but reduces implementation complexity. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
